      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-22T16:00:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why `u64`?  Can this be `u32`?  [The spec](https://www.w3.org/TR/png-3/#5Chunk-layout) uses 4 bytes for chunk length (and even augments this further by saying \"Although encoders and decoders should treat the length as unsigned, its value shall not exceed 2^31-1 bytes.\")",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 435,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 435,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "929fc0961e714fe80b0e2b3a3c4a6f25d50ce7eb",
